    "summary": "Monster Not Fade Away, stellar Black Peter, solid mid‑set",
    "blurb": "The set shines with a monster Not Fade Away and a soaring Black Peter. Jerry’s guitar solo on Not Fade Away and the strong keyboard work in The Other One stand out, while the drum duo delivers an engaging solo. I Know You Rider provides a bright lead before the show winds down.",
    "review": "On December 21, 1969 at the Fillmore Auditorium the Dead delivered a tight single‑set that still feels fresh. A brief ride into I Know You Rider segues into a haunting Black Peter, then erupts into a monster Not Fade Away where Jerry’s guitar solo is nothing short of electrifying. The band rolls straight into Good Lovin' and launches into an expansive drum duet that feeds directly into a powerful, keyboard‑rich The Other One—Tom Constanten (and Pigpen) weaving textures that lift the jam to another level. Though the show drops a bit on the final Cumberland Blues, the energy stays high and the set closes with a genuine thank‑you from Jerry, making this a memorable snapshot of the late‑’60s Dead.",
